WEBVTT

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.100
Pardon us.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.000
Hello, Shoko.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.870
It's been a while.

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:14.180
What's the matter? Why the frightened look?

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.380
If their own father directed a squad to attack their workplace,

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:19.350
anyone would look worried.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.620
I believe I warned you many times.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:26.250
"Stop involving yourself with Deava. It's dangerous."

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.120
You don't know when to listen.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.530
And if I don't listen, you'll kill me, even though I'm your own daughter?

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:32.860
You misunderstand.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:36.260
I haven't thought of killing you even once.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:41.200
However, Deava must be crushed.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:41.200
"Obey"

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.540
Shoko, do it now!

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.540
--Dad!
--Hey!

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:46.210
Don't shoot! Lower your weapon!

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:48.900
Dad, come to your senses!

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:52.880
"Obey"

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:58.750
Shoko... Why are you here?

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:00.390
Dad!

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:04.790
I... What have I been doing?

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:09.130
I can't believe it! Someone really was controlling him!

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:13.500
Captain Sakamoto, I was surprised that you and Shoko knew each other.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.500
Thank you for your assistance.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:20.910
Mr. Sakamoto was a member of my father's security detail until last year.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:24.480
Sakurako, had you noticed?

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:27.520
About Shoko's power.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:26.480
"Obey"

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.090
I only became sure of it just now.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:33.990
The special ability to absorb the power of writing and make it her own.

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:36.020
Zero Verbalism Ability.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:37.430
Zero...

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:42.030
That aside, now we have a chance to retaliate.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:43.660
All that's left...

00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:52.610
An announcement has gone out from the government.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:56.510
You and the members of Deava should be cleared of any suspicion of terrorism.

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:58.450
Now...

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:01.550
...show me what you can do, using your own methods.

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:03.040
Yes, sir.

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:08.220
Come with me.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:12.220
I will show you the truth of that moonlit night.

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:24.570
<i>The world is engulfed by an unvoiced scream</i>

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:30.510
<i>and I wait for it to reach and stir</i> <i>a certain someone's heart</i>

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:36.320
<i>With strength flowing to the edges of our souls</i>

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:42.590
<i>we set out into the white</i> <i>morning haze, without hesitation</i>

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:45.530
<i>I want to know everything about you</i>

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:55.530
<i>But just when I thought</i>
<i>I had you, you were gone</i>

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:04.610
<i>It's love, affection, passion, expression</i>

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:11.220
<i>These tightly-sealed, silent lips</i>

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:15.590
<i>gently reply back in kind</i>

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:19.860
<i>And with love, affection, passion, expression</i>

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:26.370
<i>Now, from the last of the words I couldn't find,</i>

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:35.070
<i>the music begins</i>

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:49.990
"Revive! The Vow Beneath the Moonlight"

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:52.230
I believe many of you here will be seeing me for the first time.

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:56.060
I am a second year in Seisou's
School of Politics and Economics,

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:57.330
Hayato Kujyo.

00:03:57.330 --> 00:04:00.500
I am a member of the Division of Earth Verbalism Ability, Deava.

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:05.470
What I'm about to tell you is likely to sound utterly absurd.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.910
However, it is entirely true.

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:12.580
Firstly, we at Deava have been keeping a huge secret from all of you.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:15.480
That is the crisis that threatens written civilization!

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:18.620
Think back to the past few months.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:23.420
There have been mysterious incidents inexplicable to modern science.

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:27.600
Every one of them resulted from the corrosion of a written word.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.670
The group founded to prevent that corrosion, and protect our world

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.500
is us, Deava.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:38.270
We have fought all this time to protect writing.

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:39.440
Hayato?

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:44.280
There's a reason we've kept something so important from you for so long.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:49.280
It is because we didn't trust any of you.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:51.450
If we said anything, it would only incite panic.

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:55.820
Most people lack the courage to stand against a crisis.

00:04:55.820 --> 00:05:00.460
As such, it was thought more efficient to do things with a select few.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:02.360
I thought that way, as well.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:04.330
He's as harsh as ever.

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:08.140
However, that may have been hubris on our part.

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:12.740
We overcame many crises, winning time and again, but...

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:17.340
...in the battle the other day, we lost a precious comrade.

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:23.320
At a time like this, a considerate person might say,

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:25.820
"Even in death, his soul remains with us.

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:28.760
He lives on in our hearts.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:32.330
Even if we are separated, we can be together again someday."

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:34.330
But...!

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:38.230
That can't be right! Death is the end!

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:39.600
The "soul"?

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:43.940
Even if an unproven, immaterial thing like that were right beside me,

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:45.670
what good would it do?!

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:48.240
It's not that he's alive in our hearts!

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.940
Our brains just remember he existed!

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:53.550
Yes, there's nothing after death.

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:55.850
We've only lost here.

00:05:55.850 --> 00:06:00.420
He made us laugh and supported us emotionally.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:04.930
He was larger than life, irreplaceable to us, and now he's gone.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:08.100
And so, as we are now,

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:11.070
we lack the power to fight on alone!

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:13.700
What we've lost will never come back to us.

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:17.300
However, we need to compensate for what we're now lacking.

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:23.380
We need comrades to fight at our side!

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:29.280
I know this is selfish of us to ask, having hid the truth all this time!

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:31.390
Even so, I ask of you!

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:34.620
Please, lend Deava your strength!

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:38.250
Fight alongside us! Please!

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:54.240
What a hot guy.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:55.740
I know, right?

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:57.410
Hayato...

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:03.920
Tsutomu Domon... Hayato Kujyo...

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:07.020
Their voices will save many people.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:08.920
But... I...

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:12.930
"Electricity"

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:23.700
Ready! Pull!

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:25.870
You can do it!

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:27.440
Pull!

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:29.780
We aren't done yet! Pull!

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:31.150
Pull!

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:33.640
For Hayato...

00:07:57.970 --> 00:07:59.570
Akira...

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:06.680
Can I save them as I am now?

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:08.180
Huh?

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:10.980
Vector-4? Who's piloting it?

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:14.260
Zero Verbalism Ability.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:18.530
If that's my power, I should be able to do this.

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:20.030
Swimsuits!

00:08:20.030 --> 00:08:22.830
Let me ask you to hear this trivial story of mine.

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:26.670
I'm going to bring them back.
All the smiles in the world.

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:28.340
Because, right here,

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:33.040
this place is overflowing with Tsutomu's voice!

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:35.340
Verbalize!

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:37.510
I am Shoko Iwagami!

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:37.510
"Voice I.D.

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:37.510
Shoko Iwagami"

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:42.850
The smiling woman that Tsutomu brought back!

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:51.020
Akira Kaibuki, heading out!

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:59.530
You once said

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:02.900
that the me who saved you that moonlit night is gone now.

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:08.710
But what if that person never existed at all?

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:09.880
Huh?

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:13.050
It was vague, but I had the same memory.

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:16.820
A memory of stretching out my hand to you that night.

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:18.150
However,

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:21.420
when I awakened the power of the Book of Verbalism,

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:23.820
the falsehood inside of me disappeared.

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:26.890
I realized that memory had been fabricated.

00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:28.560
A false memory?

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:30.060
Open!

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:30.120
"Open"

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:38.240
Back then, Dad implanted false memories in both of us.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:42.410
With this machine controlled by Verbalism.

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:44.110
Why would he do that?

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:49.240
I think the reason for that may lie in your true memories.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:54.760
Sousei Gattai.

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:55.790
Dash!

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:57.260
Sousei Gattai.

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:58.660
Bloom beautifully!

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:03.930
--Aquarion!
--Aquarion!!

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:11.010
"Jin"

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:11.670
--Jin!
--Jin!

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:17.170
--Rin!
--Rin!

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:16.540
"Rin"

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:22.220
Electricity.

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:21.820
"Electricity"

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:25.120
"Electricity"

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:40.640
You're so kind.

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:44.340
I just happen to be interested in why Dad did what he did.

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:47.310
How about I take a guess at why you're really doing this?

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:51.310
You're still attached to that puppet.

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:54.350
But, in order to reach your goal,

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:56.680
you have to treat her as a tool.

00:10:56.680 --> 00:10:59.720
To convince yourself she's just a soulless tool,

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:03.820
this is a little act you're putting on for yourself.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:06.650
Be silent.

00:11:25.210 --> 00:11:26.450
This is...

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:28.350
It's coming! We've succeeded!

00:11:28.350 --> 00:11:32.450
That girl is the key to the evolution of human communication.

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:34.290
She's practically a goddess.

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:37.220
Now, a world without conflict will soon come!

00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:38.460
Yes.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:39.950
Ah...

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:46.200
I was born empty.

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:48.040
Well, do you like it?

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:49.700
Yeah, this is fun.

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:51.470
Even though she's just been born,

00:11:51.470 --> 00:11:55.710
her intellect and motor skills are greater than an average ten-year-old's.

00:11:55.710 --> 00:12:01.250
I think she was born with abilities matching Subete, who called her.

00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:02.920
It's fascinating.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:05.250
Why was I born?

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:07.590
Why was I here?

00:12:07.590 --> 00:12:12.120
I didn't know, and so I just lived the life that was given to me.

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:14.330
Ta-dah!

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:16.560
Maia Tsukigane?

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:19.070
Yes, that's your name.

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:24.610
"Maia Tsukigane"

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:21.340
I'd feel bad referring to you by a number.

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:24.570
The day you were born just happened to be the full moon.

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:26.970
And there's your silver hair, as well.

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:30.140
That's why you're Tsukigane.
It's pretty and adorable.

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:31.580
I don't get it.

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:33.250
Oh... She doesn't like it?

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:38.250
"Maia Tsukigane"

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:35.920
Hey, I tried to tell you it was too straightforward.

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:38.250
A name is nothing more than a signifier, anyway.

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:40.420
No, no. Names are important.

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:42.420
I may not have understood anything,

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:47.090
but I think I felt a sense of satisfaction with my life back then.

00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:50.100
It's been a while! Hey, remember me?

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:52.970
I brought you into this world!

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:56.300
What's wrong?

00:12:56.300 --> 00:12:58.500
You're yucky.

00:13:00.310 --> 00:13:01.840
What do you make of it?

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:05.450
Nesta's memories are likely influencing her.

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:08.020
Feeling a sense of revulsion about her fated partner, huh?

00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:10.320
She's in for a hard time.

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:12.520
You're really going to buy them for me?

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:15.820
It's a pain to wash your clothes when you only have one set.

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:19.960
Besides, Nesta will foot the bill.
It's not me buying them for you.

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:19.630
"New works for the summer. Paris collection

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:19.630
now on display in the 6F Event Hall. Now,

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:19.630
you can be reborn as a mermaid. This year's

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:19.630
swimsuits are big. The summer suit revolution.

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:19.630
Yes, sweat is your friend at work!"

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:23.800
How does it look?

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:25.500
That looks good!

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:27.330
Yeah, it's cute.

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:28.740
Thank you!

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:30.300
Hey, now...

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:35.310
Ah. What's that?

00:13:35.310 --> 00:13:37.580
Oh, this is for my kid.

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:39.250
He'll be five soon.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:41.250
It's cute!

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:42.250
Isn't it?

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:45.650
"Days like this will probably go on forever."

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:47.990
That's what I thought at the time.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:56.730
Could you explain, perhaps?

00:13:56.730 --> 00:14:00.000
We were unsure of your intentions, given how little you tell us,

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:03.840
so we deciphered the writing civilization's relics independently!

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:06.010
If what's written here is true,

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:10.010
it would mean Maia was created to destroy modern civilization!

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:12.180
She's no goddess!

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:15.450
She's a devil who will destroy the world!

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:20.390
Tell me I'm mistaken, President Kenzaki!

00:14:20.390 --> 00:14:22.920
You're not wrong.

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:27.860
Destroying modern civilization and allowing people to truly be connected.

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:30.230
That is my goal.

00:14:30.230 --> 00:14:33.930
By losing that girl who is Nesta's flesh,

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:37.740
the Logos World's balance has begun to crumble.

00:14:37.740 --> 00:14:41.480
In a few years' time, distortions will begin to appear.

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:46.410
That will be when the concepts behind written words can be erased,

00:14:46.410 --> 00:14:50.050
and my project will begin in earnest.

00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:51.290
That's horrible...

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:53.890
It's too late for you to do anything.

00:14:53.890 --> 00:14:57.790
Now that that girl is here, written civilization is doomed.

00:14:57.790 --> 00:14:59.330
You were using her for something like that?!

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:00.830
Destroy.

00:15:00.390 --> 00:15:00.950
"Destroy"

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:07.770
Maia...

00:15:07.770 --> 00:15:09.260
Come with me!

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:23.080
What you were saying...

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:28.920
If I kill her, she may return to a spirit form and go back to the Logos World!

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:31.660
That must be it! Surely!

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:33.130
S-Sto--

00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:34.630
I'm sorry!

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:39.800
If I let you live, the world ends!

00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:42.500
I'm sorry, Maia!

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:45.700
I have a family to--

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:55.120
Obstacle eliminated. Recovering the target.

00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:06.890
It deflected it?!

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:09.700
A magnetic net using electromagnetic induction?

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:12.370
I-I'll Gattai and fight with you!

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:13.800
Not with that arm, you can't!

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:13.830
"Voice I.D.

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:13.830
Hayato Kujyo"

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:19.400
<i>Un, deux, trois</i>!
<i>Un, deux, trois</i>! <i>Un, deux, trois</i>!!

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:22.680
Why, you...!

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:26.070
We did it?!

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:31.990
--Karan!
--Karan!

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:37.310
Huh? Why?!

00:16:38.190 --> 00:16:40.250
Over here, M.J.B.K.!

00:16:48.370 --> 00:16:50.770
Someone! Someone, save me!

00:16:50.770 --> 00:16:53.940
Save... me...

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:57.510
"Electricity"

00:17:00.610 --> 00:17:02.580
The written characters connected.

00:17:02.720 --> 00:17:04.710
"Electricity"

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:08.260
Hey, how long are we keeping these kids around?

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:10.420
I hear we're looking for people to take them in.

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:12.860
None of them have relatives, apparently.

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:16.860
We only gathered them here in case Subete failed.

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:19.630
Yeah, we don't need the spares anymore.

00:17:24.570 --> 00:17:27.910
Hey, you have to go to sleep, or they'll get mad!

00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:30.380
Hey, listen!

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:31.980
The girl escaped!

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:33.470
What?!

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:40.590
Is someone there?

00:17:40.590 --> 00:17:42.760
Who are you?

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:45.960
Don't be scared. I won't do anything to you.

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:47.730
Liar.

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:50.230
'Cause he told me...

00:17:50.230 --> 00:17:53.230
...that I can't be allowed to live...

00:17:53.230 --> 00:17:55.240
That's not true.

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:59.310
He said that if I live, the world will end!

00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:01.240
Everyone will die!

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:05.010
I don't want that! I don't!

00:18:05.010 --> 00:18:09.750
It won't end. The world won't end, even if you live.

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:11.520
You're lying.

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:14.420
I'm not! It won't ever end!

00:18:14.420 --> 00:18:17.620
Liar! How can you say that?!

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:21.630
If it really looks like the world will end because of you,

00:18:21.630 --> 00:18:22.960
I'll save it!

00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:25.430
That's right! I'll become the savior!

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:28.370
Savior...?

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:31.440
I'll stop the end of the world for you.

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:34.970
So, don't worry! It's okay for you to live!

00:18:45.650 --> 00:18:47.450
I see...

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:49.990
The one who saved me was...

00:18:49.990 --> 00:18:55.630
That void I always felt inside me... It was you.

00:18:55.630 --> 00:18:57.330
Let me go!

00:18:57.330 --> 00:18:59.300
Dad! What is this?!

00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:01.670
Verbalize.

00:19:01.670 --> 00:19:03.870
Don't forget! I'm going to save it!

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:06.340
I'll become the savior! It'll all be okay!

00:19:06.340 --> 00:19:07.740
Yeah! Yeah!

00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:09.970
I am Akira, your--

00:19:13.810 --> 00:19:19.020
Confine Maia's activities to the training facility and living area from now on.

00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:21.890
I will handle her education personally.

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:22.890
Huh?

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:26.260
This should maintain the bare minimum connection she needs with Subete.

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:28.100
We don't require anything beyond that.

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:32.100
Living life like a normal person will only hurt Maia eventually.

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:35.370
Maia? Is that the girl's name?

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:39.830
Yes. It was the least I could do.

00:19:40.510 --> 00:19:47.180
"Kaibuki"

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:43.240
You must be Akira.

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:47.110
We've gone so long without being blessed with a child.

00:19:47.110 --> 00:19:51.690
So, we hope you'll think of us as your father and mother.

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:54.690
Maybe that's being too pushy, though.

00:19:54.690 --> 00:19:56.620
I... I will...

00:19:56.620 --> 00:19:58.360
What is it?

00:19:58.360 --> 00:20:01.700
I will become the savior... no matter what...

00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:03.130
Why?

00:20:03.130 --> 00:20:06.070
I don't know. I can't remember!

00:20:06.070 --> 00:20:09.640
But I have to become the savior!

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:14.110
When a man talks about his dreams, he doesn't do it with tears in his eyes.

00:20:14.110 --> 00:20:16.410
Instead, give those feelings voice.

00:20:16.410 --> 00:20:20.550
Don't say you'll become the savior someday.
Say that you're that now!

00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:22.720
To yourself. And to others.

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:24.750
I am the savior.

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:31.160
Good. A voice imbued with an unshakable will can give you true power.

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:32.820
I●●●

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:37.000
I●●●

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:38.490
...will save you!

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:44.400
--Huh?!
--What?!

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:45.940
What is this?

00:20:45.940 --> 00:20:48.840
I've lost control of my machine!

00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:50.330
Sousei Gattai!

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:53.010
Save!

00:20:53.010 --> 00:21:00.940
Aquarion!

00:21:04.420 --> 00:21:06.690
Deava!

00:21:04.420 --> 00:21:05.830
"Heaven"

00:21:06.690 --> 00:21:09.630
I will never forget again!

00:21:09.630 --> 00:21:11.870
--H-Huh?
--Why?

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:13.800
Our cockpits are the same as for our vectors.

00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:15.290
Kaibuki?

00:21:33.050 --> 00:21:35.360
Lightning Speed!

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:34.790
"Lightning Speed"

00:21:35.360 --> 00:21:38.150
I am Akira, your...

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:42.150
I am Maia's...

00:21:59.010 --> 00:22:00.670
...savior!

00:22:16.330 --> 00:22:20.830
I have to go back... to where Akira is.

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:26.770
<i>I want to lend you a true voice</i>

00:22:36.850 --> 00:22:42.190
<i>With the warmth of salvation,</i>
<i>I raise my hand into the sky</i>

00:22:42.190 --> 00:22:46.930
<i>and everything in the world gains its true colors</i>

00:22:46.930 --> 00:22:49.600
<i>(Focus) A sound that was once hidden</i>

00:22:49.600 --> 00:22:52.700
<i>(on the goal) will connect us now</i>

00:22:52.700 --> 00:22:55.200
<i>Try to understand that, okay?</i>

00:22:55.200 --> 00:22:57.640
<i>So, are you ready?</i>

00:22:57.640 --> 00:23:00.440
<i>(heart and soul) These silent teardrops</i>

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:03.040
<i>(narrow escape) that flow forth now</i>

00:23:03.040 --> 00:23:06.550
<i>(enamored) are proof of that person's existence</i>

00:23:06.550 --> 00:23:13.050
<i>You can't go inside your heart all alone</i>

00:23:13.050 --> 00:23:15.620
<i>I will hesitate no more</i>

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:20.790
<i>I want to lend you a true voice</i>

00:23:20.790 --> 00:23:26.000
<i>A useful life, a sparkling utopia</i>

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:35.110
<i>When your heart and voice</i> <i>tremble together, you'll surpass all</i>

00:23:35.110 --> 00:23:38.510
<i>So go for your heart</i>

00:23:51.430 --> 00:23:54.660
A long, long time ago, there were two sisters: Hanako and Kaguya.

00:23:54.660 --> 00:23:56.330
I h-have fond memories of that script.

00:23:56.330 --> 00:23:58.430
Hey, how long ago is "long, long ago"? The Showa Period?

00:23:58.430 --> 00:23:59.530
The Heian Period.

00:23:59.530 --> 00:24:01.770
A thousand years ago, huh?
Writing sure is amazing!

00:24:01.770 --> 00:24:03.300
How long ago is a thousand years?

00:24:03.300 --> 00:24:05.970
One twelfth of 12,000 years ago.

00:24:05.970 --> 00:24:07.440
Now I get it even less!

00:24:07.440 --> 00:24:08.610
Episode 24!

00:24:07.970 --> 00:24:10.830
"Episode 24: To Battle!

00:24:07.970 --> 00:24:10.830
With My Existence on the Line"

00:24:08.610 --> 00:24:10.780
"To Battle! With My Existence on the Line."
